{"chunk_id": "e433ba61d877", "text": "Sita, declaring her unwavering fidelity to Rama and calling upon the cosmic Witness, enters the blazing fire to prove her purity before the assembled armies, sages, gods, and common people. The crowd erupts in grief as she vanishes into the flames like a sacred offering. As Rama stands sorrowful, the greatest gods\u2014Indra, Yama, Varuna, Mahadeva, and Brahma\u2014arrive in radiant chariots. They rebuke Rama for acting as though he were merely human and reveal his true identity. At Rama\u2019s own request for clarity, Brahma proclaims the cosmic truth: Rama is none other than Narayana/Vishnu, the eternal Supreme Being who incarnated to destroy Ravana. Sita is Lakshmi herself. With Ravana slain, the divine mission is complete. The scene transforms the epic from heroic war story into cosmic revelation, declaring Rama\u2019s divine nature and the theological meaning of his incarnation.\nAfter Sita enters the fire, the gods arrive and Brahma reveals that Rama is the divine Vishnu incarnate who came to slay Ravana.\nThemes: divine identity, avatara revelation, cosmic praise, Sita's trial by fire, gods acknowledging Rama", "vector": [0.0007726144976913929, -0.02225392498075962, -0.009044761769473553, 0.010798539035022259, -0.02255607396364212, -0.006706391926854849, -0.03307873755693436, -0.015974480658769608, -0.023278603330254555, -0.006883740425109863, 0.023672711104154587, 0.017248760908842087, 0.009747586213052273, 0.011770670302212238, -0.010437274351716042, 0.005832787603139877, 0.04190674051642418, -0.013327394612133503, 0.026864979416131973, -0.009327205829322338, -0.006621002219617367, -0.02071690559387207, -0.01424040924757719, 0.02724594995379448, -0.032343070954084396, -0.007225300185382366, 0.024592293426394463, -0.03397204726934433, 0.027088306844234467, -0.020099470391869545, -0.012059682980179787, -0.004522380884736776, -0.004936193581670523, -0.006351695396006107, -0.017918743193149567, 0.0013087645638734102, -0.004